acceptanceCriteria.text:
The context inventory names both native body entry points: MBAgentVisuals.AddSkinMeshes (callers Agent.AddSkinMeshes, AgentVisuals.AddSkinMeshesToEntity) and MBAgentVisuals.FillEntityWithBodyMeshesWithoutAgentVisuals (caller BasicCharacterTableau, the save/load preview). It lists every caller site with its identity source:
- mission agents: IMissionListener.OnEquipItemsFromSpawnEquipment;
- single-player 3D tableaus: AgentVisualsData.CharacterObjectStringIdData, already set from CharacterViewModel.CharStringId on the CharacterDeveloper, Clan, Encyclopedia, Inventory, Party and Tournament screens; map party icons likewise;
- 2D thumbnails: the CharacterCode token, plus a prefix on CharacterSpawner.InitWithCharacter (or CharacterThumbnailCache.FillEntityWithPose) that copies the parsed token into AgentVisualsData.CharacterObjectStringId, because InitWithCharacter builds its data from CharacterCode fields only;
- MapConversationTableau.SpawnOpponentLeader and SpawnOpponentBodyguardCharacter: a prefix;
- the save/load preview (per D18, decided at the sprint-1 checkpoint through MMR-265; recommended: (a) patched, if U5 shows the material override holds on that entity, otherwise (b) native-only);
- the eight AgentVisuals.Create callers listed in a8, none of which sets CharacterObjectStringId.

The inventory lists the eight AgentVisuals.Create callers, none of which sets CharacterObjectStringId, with their identity sources:
- CharacterCreationNarrativeStageView.SpawnHumanNarrativeMenuCharacter, CharacterCreationOptionsStageView.AddCharacterEntity, CharacterCreationReviewStageView.AddCharacterEntity and CharacterCreationClanNamingStageView.AddCharacterEntity (source: the pre-campaign creator record, MMR-178 a7);
- BannerEditorView.AddCharacterEntity, GauntletBannerBuilderScreen.AddCharacterEntities, GauntletEducationScreen.RefreshSceneCharacters and GauntletSceneNotification.OpenScene (source: the shown hero's StringId; a site with no campaign hero is handled (per D22, decided at the sprint-1 checkpoint through MMR-265; recommended: (b) read-only authored records)).

tickets.body:
Record the user's decision for every sprint-1 result that failed, was blocked, limited or unresolved, and for every decision deferred to the sprint-1 checkpoint. Prerequisite: sprint-1 acceptance (MMR-129), enforced by the sprint boundary. MMR-167 waits for this ticket.

For each such result, show the user the evidence, the affected success criteria and four options with cost: (1) an alternative mechanism as bounded sprint-2 or sprint-3 work, including promoting a people that is still a delta (hill dwarf, frosthold dwarf or a human people) to its own Bannerlord race beside the five D14 races; (2) re-pin the game build; (3) move the requirement to a named follow-up epic; (4) accept a named narrower behaviour. Results in scope: key capacity path C (MMR-165), the per-hero bake route and the shader route (MMR-163), DCC runtime load (MMR-217), small-scale combat agents for the gnome race at about 0.53-0.58 scale (U14), native acceptance of the four added races elf, dwarf, gnome and tidekin (U15), the bone_scale range for a people that stays a delta (U16), the tidekin nictitating-lid channel (U30), and the D2 art pipeline if MMR-264's import or remake failed.

Also present the sprint-1-checkpoint decisions with their options and recommendations:
- D5 family race (recommended: (a), creation-time family takes the player's race and children take the same-sex parent's race);
- D6 race lifespans (recommended: B, display-scaled);
- D7 distant figures (recommended: (a), a frozen distant-appearance subset that the battle-scale epic consumes);
- D8 shader-route fallback (recommended: probe (a); if it fails, choose (c), not (b));
- D9 named narrowings (recommended: bust (a); walk style to a follow-up animation epic);
- D11 breadth targets (recommended: (a), the round-2-verified DD2 GUI counts, plus the user's own targets for the four unverified families);
- D13 DCC fallback (recommended: re-scope s13 to key compatibility);
- D18 save/load preview (recommended: (a) if U5 holds on the preview entity, otherwise (b));
- D19 voice and BodyWeightData (recommended: (a), out of scope as a user-approved narrowing);
- D20 child and teen quality bar (recommended: (a), the MMR-266 benchmark pair);
- D21 hair physics (recommended: (a), static hair);
- D22 non-campaign modes (recommended: (b), read-only authored records);
- D23 ProceduralWorld seam direction (recommended: (a), a provider interface landed with the FWGC epic owner).
Also present the MMR-264 benchmark for the user's verdict: the player head pair and the ordinary-NPC cohort with its notable or townsperson, in the DD2-derived and AI-remake forms beside vanilla.

This ticket never launches the game. It records the user's answers and never invents one.

Execution contract: All listed output paths are proposed implementation contracts, not files already delivered. Read accepted prerequisite artifacts and the saved epic before work. Token context is an estimate. One worker owns the listed source paths; record any narrower ownership before parallel edits. One integration owner exclusively controls the shared Bannerlord/DD2/editor/import state and packaged assets under CLAIM/RELEASE, with the process check before each editor session; queue imports, and every handoff records build identities, saved/dirty state and in-flight work. This ticket never launches the game: every in-game or capture result is written as fail-soft probe steps, desk-checked here, and run by the sprint's acceptance node in its one live round. Per-ticket checks are: it compiles, existing suites pass, and targeted assertions cover new pure logic. Evidence identifies exact source, game, asset, catalog, settings and test inputs. Missing required capability or failed checks block dependent work; keep independent work moving. No placeholders, skipped required entries or unsupported-as-complete outcomes. Do not modify unrelated epics.
